  "reason": "With zero completed experiments, there is no performance reference point, making every subsequent result uninterpretable. The most critical first question is: what is the baseline performance of the simplest viable model? config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the most minimal configuration—no image modality, no multi-profile aggregation, no fusion—so it isolates the core RNA classification pipeline with a standard, well-understood encoder. Establishing this baseline is essential before any multimodal or image-only result can be meaningfully compared. It reduces the largest source of uncertainty (the absolute performance scale) with a single run, and it provides the anchor against which all later experiments (image-only, multimodal, different encoders, aggregation strategies) will be judged. Under a tight budget, spending the first experiment on a clean, interpretable baseline maximizes the information gained per run and prevents misattribution of gains or losses in later, more complex configurations."
}

